# DesignCheck — API keys
#
# Copy this file to a new file named `.env.local` in the same folder, fill
# in real values, then restart `npm run dev` (or redeploy on Vercel).
# `.env.local` is already git-ignored — never commit real keys.
#
# You do NOT need either of these to try the app — click "Try Demo" on the
# home page to see a full example with no setup at all.

# 1) Figma personal access token — required for real (non-demo) analysis.
#    Without this, DesignCheck only runs in Demo Mode.
#
#    How to get one:
#    1. Go to https://www.figma.com and log in.
#    2. Click your avatar (top-left) → Settings.
#    3. Open the "Security" tab.
#    4. Scroll to "Personal access tokens" → click "Generate new token".
#    5. Give it any name (e.g. "DesignCheck"), click Generate.
#    6. Copy the token immediately — Figma only shows it once.
#    7. Paste it below, after the "=" sign, with no quotes and no spaces.
FIGMA_TOKEN=

# 2) Google Gemini API key — OPTIONAL. Used only to generate a friendlier,
#    one-sentence "why this matters" explanation for each issue. Every
#    measurement (colors, spacing, text, sizes) works perfectly without
#    this — it's a nice-to-have, not a requirement.
#
#    How to get one (free, no credit card):
#    1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com
#    2. Click "Get API key" → "Create API key".
#    3. Copy the key and paste it below.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override which Gemini model is used (defaults to a fast,
# low-cost model). Check https://ai.google.dev/models if this is retired.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
